lity of squared() – applying it twice results in the fourth power of the original values.'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.squared() - empty delegate', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'Calling getValue(0) on the squared indicator throws IndexOutOfBoundsException because the underlying delegate contains no bars.', 'description': 'Validate behaviour when the original indicator has an empty BarSeries (no data points). The squared() call should not fail during creation but any attempt to read a value must respect the empty series.'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.squared() - mixed values', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator where getValue(i) = original.getValue(i) * original.getValue(i) for each index i. For a delegate returning [0, -3, 5, -1.2] the squared values are [0, 9, 25, 1.44] (within Num precision).', 'description': 'Ensure that squared() correctly handles a mixture of zero, negative, positive and fractional numbers in a single series.'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.squared() - large numbers', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator where getValue(i) = original.getValue(i) * original.getValue(i). For a delegate returning [10000000000] the squared value is [100000000000000000000] (1e20) without overflow.', 'description': 'Verify that the implementation works with very large numeric values supported by the Num implementation and does not overflow.'}]}, {'group': 'NumericIndicator.squared() - bar series propagation', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': "The BarSeries returned by squared().getBarSeries() is the same instance as the original NumericIndicator's BarSeries.", 'description': 'Check that squared() forwards the BarSeries reference unchanged, preserving series context for downstream rules.'}, {'input': [], 'expected': "The unstable bars count returned by squared().getUnstableBars() equals the original indicator's unstable bars count.", 'description': 'Confirm that the unstable bars metadata is propagated unchanged by 